{"topicSections":[{"title":"The clock","anchor":"The-clock","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock","doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock\/Text"]},{"title":"Times of day","anchor":"Times-of-day","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/TimeOfDay","doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/TimeFormat"]},{"title":"An actor’s day","anchor":"An-actors-day","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Timetable","doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Stop"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Extended Modules","anchor":"Extended-Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Gnusto"]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"GnustoClock","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"GnustoClock"}],"role":"collection","title":"GnustoClock"},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An adventure counts moves. A mystery counts minutes: every alibi in the house"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is stated as a time, and a player who cannot check one against a clock is being"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"asked to take the game’s word for it. This library gives the move counter an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hour and a minute, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"},{"type":"text","text":" verb that reads it back, alarms that go off at a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stated hour, and timetables that keep an actor where his day says he is."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The clock is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"derived, not ticked"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock\/now","type":"reference"},{"text":" is a pure function of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"engine’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"moves","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so every rule, action, fuse and daemon in one turn reads the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same time, the timer tick that closes the turn included. A clock advanced by a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"daemon of its own would be read differently by daemons sorting before and after","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it, which would make the hour depend on other timers’ names. Deriving also","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"inherits the engine’s own notion of world time: the hour doesn’t move on a parse","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"error or a meta command, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"take all","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" costs one turn rather than four.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock"},{"type":"text","text":" is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GameContent"},{"type":"text","text":" bundle rather than a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GamePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", because it has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state to keep — the minutes a game has moved the clock by hand, whether it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"paused, and which stop each scheduled actor was last seen keeping. A bundle’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"globals namespace themselves and travel in save files, so the host lists the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"clock in ","type":"text"},{"code":"content","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and gets all three for nothing. Everything else belongs to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the host: the rooms, the actors, the bodies of the alarms, and the timetables. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Timetable","type":"reference"},{"text":" holds no state of its own, which is what lets a game declare one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as an ordinary computed property naming its own rooms, and what makes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Timetable\/location(at:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" an answer available at bootstrap, in a rule, and in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a plain unit test.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Gnusto","import GnustoClock          \/\/ .product(name: \"GnustoClock\", package: \"Gnusto\")","","struct Fulminate: Game {","    let clock = Clock(startingAt: TimeOfDay(17, 30), minutesPerTurn: 2, text: clockText)","","    static let clockText: Clock.Text = {","        var text = Clock.Text()","        text.timeIs = .naming { \"Your watch says \\($0).\" }","        return text","    }()","","    var content: GameContents { clock }        \/\/ the verb, the action, the saved state","","    var timers: [TimedEvent] {","        clock.schedule(teague, named: \"teague.day\", teagueDay)","","        clock.at(TimeOfDay(17, 46), named: \"clock.blast\") {","            blastHappened = true","        }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reading the time needs a live turn, so "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock\/now","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" belongs in a rule body, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"describe"},{"type":"text","text":" block, an action or a timer, and not in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":" block, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"evaluated at bootstrap. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":" block that wants to place a scheduled actor asks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the timetable instead, which reads no world state:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"teague.starts(in: teagueDay.location(at: clock.start))"},{"type":"text","text":". A stored clock also"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hands the play-test status footer a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time=5:46 pm"},{"type":"text","text":" field, which a timed game"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wants, since a line true at half past five and false at six reads the same in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transcript that never says which it was."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Puts a wall clock over the engine’s turn counter, so a game can be played"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"against an evening rather than a move count."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnustoclock"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/TimeOfDay":{"kind":"symbol","title":"TimeOfDay","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TimeOfDay","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/timeofday","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/TimeOfDay","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TimeOfDay","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A time on a 24-hour wall clock, with no date attached: 8:15 in the evening","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimeOfDay(20, 15)"},{"text":", and it is the same value tomorrow.","type":"text"}]},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/Stop":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Stop","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/stop","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Stop","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Stop"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One appointment on an actor’s day: where they are meant to be, from when."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Stop","type":"topic"},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/TimeFormat":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/TimeFormat","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/timeformat","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TimeFormat"}],"type":"topic","title":"TimeFormat","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/TimeOfDay"},{"type":"text","text":" is spelled for the player."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TimeFormat"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/Clock/Text":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock\/Text","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/clock\/text","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Text"}],"type":"topic","title":"Clock.Text","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The clock’s own voice: the one line the mechanics print. Override the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"line at init to re-skin; the clock stores its table as a "},{"code":"let","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so init"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is the only chance."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/Clock":{"kind":"symbol","title":"Clock","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Clock"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/clock","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Clock"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A wall clock over the turn counter: a game where it is twenty to six, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ten to six four turns later.","type":"text"}]},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/Gnusto":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Gnusto","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/gnusto","type":"topic","title":"Gnusto","abstract":[],"role":"collection"},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock":{"kind":"symbol","title":"GnustoClock","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Puts a wall clock over the engine’s turn counter, so a game can be played"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"against an evening rather than a move count."}]},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/Clock/now":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock\/now","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/clock\/now","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"now"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11GnustoClock9TimeOfDayV","text":"TimeOfDay"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"What time it is now.","type":"text"}],"title":"now","type":"topic"},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/Timetable":{"kind":"symbol","title":"Timetable","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Timetable"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/timetable","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Timetable","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Timetable"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An actor’s day, written down: a list of stops the clock walks them through."}]},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/Timetable/location(at:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Timetable\/location(at:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/timetable\/location(at:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"location"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"at"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11GnustoClock9TimeOfDayV","text":"TimeOfDay"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8LocationV","text":"Location"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Where the actor is — or was, or will be — at a given time.","type":"text"}],"title":"location(at:)","type":"topic"}}}